"critique":"The dialogue stage has a severe, jarring layout failure: the text is broken into a single-word-per-line vertical column (\"like / company. / And / the / guard?\") with a vertical rule running through it, indicating a missing or broken text container width. This is the most glaring craft defect on screen. The header is inconsistent: the \"Objective reached\" pill uses a bright gold border and fill that clashes with the muted, low-contrast gold of the Gold/Renown counters, and the third counter (\"NIGHTFALL\") is clipped/cut off at the right edge, breaking the header's symmetry and grid. The three top-level panels (Townsfolk, Stage, Quest Log) have mismatched internal padding and header treatments: the sidebar header uses a small-caps label with a right-aligned count, the stage uses a large portrait+name block, and the quest log uses a title with a right-aligned chapter tag—none share a consistent header baseline or vertical rhythm. Portrait treatment is inconsistent: the large stage portrait has a heavy gold ring and glow, while the sidebar portraits are flat circles with no ring, and the active sidebar item (Bruno) only gets a thin left accent bar rather than matching the stage's emphasis. Status dots (green/amber/grey) are tiny and inconsistently spaced from the role text. The \"Gathered Clues\" card has a faint, almost invisible left border and a low-contrast italic body that reads as unfinished. Choice rows (1–4) have uneven right-edge alignment of the CLUE/LEAD/DANGER/LEAVE tags and inconsistent icon spacing. Overall the dark navy palette is coherent, but the gold accent is applied at too many different opacities/weights, and borders/shadows are applied inconsistently across cards.",
"suggestion":"Priority 1: Fix the dialogue text container—give it a proper max-width (e.g., 60–70% of the stage) and normal multi-line wrapping so the paragraph reads as a block; remove the stray vertical rule or convert it to a deliberate left quote-margin. Priority 2: Repair the header grid—give all three counters equal width and identical styling, un-clip the third counter, and unify the accent treatment so the \"Objective reached\" state uses the same gold as the counters (e.g., a subtle gold border + tint rather than a bright fill). Priority 3: Establish a single card/panel system: identical outer radius, border color/weight, and internal padding across all three columns; standardize panel headers to one pattern (small-caps label left, meta tag right, consistent baseline). Priority 4: Unify portrait grammar—apply the same ring/glow treatment at a smaller scale to sidebar avatars, and make the active NPC state consistent between sidebar and stage (e.g., matching gold ring + accent). Priority 5: Tighten the accent system—define 2–3 gold tokens (primary, muted, disabled) and apply them consistently to borders, tags, and icons; increase contrast on the \"Gathered Clues\" body text and give that card a visible border to match siblings. Priority 6: Align the choice-row tags to a fixed right column and standardize icon-to-text spacing for a clean, even rhythm."
}

